course: dictionary
lesson: 4041
title: Gelatine and setting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a thing and also tell you what it does. «Gelatine» is a clear substance with no taste. The words around it give clues: «Jelly sets because gelatine molecules form a loose net that traps water.» Sets means becomes firm, so gelatine helps a runny liquid turn into a wobbly solid.
explain: Look at the words around a new word. «Fresh pineapple stops jelly setting because it holds a substance that cuts gelatine.» The word stops tells you the pineapple prevents the jelly from going firm. Ask yourself what would fit in the gap, then put your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Gelatine is used in many everyday things. «Gummy sweets are made by squirting hot syrup with gelatine or pectin into shapes.» So gelatine is one of the ingredients that can give sweets their chewy shape. Notice that the sentence names two ingredients, and the word or tells you they are two choices.
fact: Gelatine is a clear substance with no taste.
fact: Gelatine is made by boiling animal bones and skin.
fact: When a liquid with gelatine in it cools, it sets into a wobbly solid.
fact: Gelatine is used to make jelly, sweets, glue, medicine capsules and photographic film.
fact: Many gummy sweets contain gelatine, so they are not suitable for vegetarians; vegetarian versions use agar from seaweed.
exercise: «Jelly sets because gelatine molecules form a loose net that traps water.» What does sets mean here? | Stays runny forever | Turns bright red | *Goes firm and wobbly as it cools | Runs out of the bowl
exercise: Gelatine is made by boiling what? | *Animal bones and skin | Sand and rock | Plants and seeds | Sugar and water
exercise: «Fresh pineapple stops jelly setting.» Why does the jelly not go firm? | The pineapple is made of gelatine | *It holds a substance that cuts gelatine | It has too much sugar in it | It is too cold in the fridge
test: Gelatine has no taste. What does "no taste" mean? | It tastes very sour like lemons | It tastes of pineapple | It tastes very sweet | *It does not have a flavour
test: Which ingredient can vegetarians use instead of gelatine? | Sheep's bones | Pig skin | *Agar from seaweed | Boiled cow hooves
exam: Why might some people avoid gummy sweets? | They are always sour | *They contain gelatine made from animals | They contain too much fruit | They are made from seaweed
